# SunnyWalker

A voice-interactive alarm clock for 7-year-olds. iOS 17+, Swift + SwiftUI, Studio-Ghibli watercolor aesthetic. 100% offline, no ads, no tracking.

## Quick start

```bash
# 1. One-time setup
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
./run.sh setup

# 2. Run today's dev cycle (~30-60 min, ~$1.60)
./run.sh today

# 3. Inspect
./run.sh status
cat orchestrator/logs/$(date +%F)/d_review.md
```

## Documents
- `docs/first_idea.md` — original concept
- `docs/swift_native_spec.md` — full Swift + SwiftUI implementation spec
- `docs/multi_agent_workflow.md` — 4-agent automation design

## The 4 AI agents
| | Role | Model | Cost/day |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | Coder — writes Swift | Sonnet 4.6 | ~$0.32 |
| B | Validator — build + test + lint | Haiku 4.5 | ~$0.02 |
| C | Reporter + CI — daily report + git | Haiku 4.5 | ~$0.03 |
| D | Reviewer — evaluate + tomorrow brief | Opus 4.6 | ~$1.20 |

## Manual scripts
- `scripts/validate.sh` — xcodebuild + tests + swiftlint
- `scripts/git_ca.sh "<msg>"` — safe commit + push to `dev/auto`
- `scripts/dev.sh build | test | lint | sim | logs | clean | branch`

## Safety rails
- AI A cannot run `git` or `xcodebuild`
- AI B cannot modify code
- AI C can only push to `dev/auto`, never `main`
- AI D is read-only
- You manually `git merge dev/auto → main` when satisfied

## Daily cadence (7-day MVP)
| Day | Theme |
|---|---|
| 1 | Project skeleton, Models, Theme |
| 2 | HomeView, AlarmListView (dummy data) |
| 3 | AlarmScheduler + notifications |
| 4 | AudioRecorder + RecordingView |
| 5 | SpeechRecognizer + AlarmRingView |
| 6 | ParentalGate + Settings + SwiftData |
| 7 | Polish + App Store assets + TestFlight |
